note SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
note omegallm serve.om (aien-train DRA-119): `ollm serve PORT CK MERGES [MAXCONN] [tplmax=N]
note [test=1]`, an OpenAI-compatible HTTP/1.1 server for a v1 BPE checkpoint (V > 256) on
note 127.0.0.1:PORT only. aarch64 only: build.sh composes it under one `om2` line after the
note omega-mv e5b32567 units net/http.om, net/json.om and net/jsonw.om (vendored unmodified); the
note other targets take noserve.om. It prints `PORT n`, then serves one request at a time, one
note request per connection (Connection: close), until MAXCONN connections (default 1000000) have
note been served. A connection is served once its first bytes arrive; a silent one waits in one
note of 8 pending slots and is closed unanswered 10 s after its accept (svwait). tplmax=N
note (256 .. 983040, default 65536) caps the chat template in bytes; test=1 enables the test-only
note members ollm_test_output and ollm_test_delay_ms (refused otherwise).
note Routes: GET /health {"status":"ok","in_flight":0,"busy":false}; GET /v1/models;
note POST /v1/chat/completions with JSON or SSE (stream true) responses; other paths 404, other
note methods 405. in_flight counts the generating chat completions (0 or 1, one slot); busy is
note in_flight 1. While a completion generates, the listener and pending connections are served
note between tokens: GET /health answers {"status":"ok","in_flight":1,"busy":true}, GET
note /v1/models the list, and every other request 503 server_busy with Retry-After: 1. A client
note that leaves (svgone) stops its generation: nothing more is sent, logged as status 499.
note Request: messages (non-empty array of objects with a string role of at most 32 bytes and a
note content that is a string, null, or an array of {"type":"text","text":string} parts joined
note with no separator; other part types are 400; content may be absent beside tool_calls),
note optional max_tokens or max_completion_tokens (1 .. 999999), temperature (0 .. 2 without
note exponent, used to 0.001; default 1), seed (unsigned, default 1), top_k (integer -1 ..
note 999999; -1, 0 and K >= V are off), top_p (0 <= p <= 1 without exponent, used to 0.000001;
note 0 keeps only the most probable token, 1 is off), stop (null, a string or an array of at most
note 8 strings of 1 .. 128 bytes), tools (array of at most 128
note {"type":"function","function":{"name":1 .. 64 bytes, ...}}), tool_choice ("none", "auto",
note "required" or a {"type":"function"} object), stream,
note stream_options.include_usage and n (only 1). Other members (model, ...) are ignored.
note Interim chat template (until DRA-123 fixes one shared template): when tools is non-empty,
note `tools: ` and the request's tools JSON text as sent, then `\n`; then `role: content\n` for
note each message in order, an assistant's tool_calls appended to its content as
note `<tool_call>{"name":NAME,"arguments":ARGS}</tool_call>` (NAME the JSON string as sent, ARGS
note the decoded string or the object's JSON text as sent, {} when absent); then `assistant: `.
note At most tplmax bytes, else 400. The context is token 0 then the template's encoding (CT0
note tokens, reported as prompt_tokens); CT0 >= T is refused with 400 context_length_exceeded
note stating CT0 and T. Output runs at most min(max_tokens, T - CT0) tokens, so the T-token window
note never slides (cmdsamp's step osstep, splitmix64 seed stream; with top_k or top_p on, the
note kept tokens are the most probable in order, ties to the lower id, up to K and until their
note mass reaches top_p, drawn by the same uniform scaled to the kept mass); a generated token 0
note ends it with finish_reason stop, the limit with length, the earliest stop string with stop
note (the content cut before it; a streamed chunk never sends a byte a stop could still claim).
note Tool calls (tools non-empty, tool_choice not "none"): when the content from the first
note `<tool_call>` on is 1 .. 8 blocks `<tool_call>{"name":N,"arguments":A}</tool_call>` with only
note whitespace between and after, N a declared tool name and A an object, a string or absent,
note the answer carries tool_calls (id call_<request>_<i>, arguments the object's JSON text or the
note string) with finish_reason tool_calls and content the text before, trailing whitespace
note dropped, null when empty; otherwise the text is plain content. Streaming holds back a
note possible marker and trailing whitespace, then sends the tool_calls in one delta chunk.
note Decoded bytes are sent as UTF-8: a sequence cut by a token boundary waits for the next token,
note an ill-formed one (or one cut by the end) becomes U+FFFD. One line per routed response (and
note per 413 at the head, and per request answered during a generation) goes to stdout: `C status
note prompt_tokens completion_tokens finish(0 none, 1 stop, 2 length, 3 tool_calls, 4 client left)
note ms`. A body over 65532 JSON tokens is 413 request_too_large.
note Exit codes: 2 usage; 27 merges (bpe.om); 71 the port cannot be bound.
note wb layout: raw token bytes [0, 8192), content [8192, 73728), stop strings [73728, 74752) (8 x
note 128), markers [74752, 74784), message [81920, 82176), response id [82176, 82240), call id
note [82240, 82432), tool names [82432, 90624) (128 x 64), template [90624, 1073664). bd holds the
note request, then the tool calls' names and arguments [0, 131072). sv slots: 0 stream, 1 max
note tokens, 2 TEMPMILLI, 3 seed state, 4 include_usage, 5 template bytes, 6 CT0, 7 generated, 8
note finish, 9 request count, 10 created, 11 start ns, 12 raw bytes, 13 content bytes, 14 content
note sent, 15 id length, 16 error code, 17 chunk end, 19 T, 21 last status, 22 test mode, 23
note tplmax, 24 forced tokens, 25 forced on, 26 test output bytes, 27 delay ms, 28 top_k, 29 top_p
note millionths, 30 tools, 31 tool detection, 32 tool calls, 33 marker position, 34 bd fill,
note 35 stop strings, 36 listen fd.

